### Tested versions

Tested with :
* v4.6.2.stable.mono.official [71f334935]
* v4.5.1.stable.mono.official [f62fdbde1]

Exported on a Meta Quest 3


### System information

Godot v4.6.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400H @ 2.70GHz (12 threads) - 23.72 GiB memory

### Issue description

#### Context
My project is an XR application on a Meta Quest 3 using OpenXR.
I wanted to extend the behavior of a node. My project is in C# and the node's script came from a tool in GDScript, so I wrapped its node by giving it a parent that would expose the properties of the child and add its own functionalities on top. Exposing the properties came by redirecting the getter and the setter of the parent properties to the child Node.

#### What happened
The scripts being marked as tools, they worked fine running in editor. Then, I ran the program in XR Mode which still worked as intended.
But when I hit the Remote Deploy button to run it on the Meta Quest 3, it appeared that all the values set in the editor were all set to null for the wrapper node and sometimes even going through the setter twice for value initialization.
Here an example of the console output I can get from the scripts provided next:
 ```console
buffering coord2D (0, 0)
buffering coord3D (0, 0, 0)
buffering coord2D (0, 0)
buffering coord3D (0, 0, 0)
Instantiated child with name WrappedNode
OpenXR initialized successfully
```


### Steps to reproduce

* Having a basic XR project able to run with an `XROrigin3D` node and a `XRCamera3D` node.
* Create a scene with 2 `Node3D` one being the wrapper and the other the one being wrapped (the problem is the same with C# wrapping GDScript and C# wrapping C#) and attaching the following scripts to them :
**Child Node**
```cs
using Godot;
using System;

[Tool]
public partial class WrappedNode : Node3D
{
    [Export]
    public Vector2 Coord2D { get; set; }

    [Export]
    public Vector3 Coord3D { get; set; }
}
```
**ParentNode**
```cs
using Godot;
using System;

[Tool]
public partial class WrappingNode : Node3D
{
    [Export]
    public Vector2 WrappedCoord2D { 
        get => _child != null ? (Vector2)_child?.Get("Coord2D") : new Vector2() ; 
        set
        {
            if(_child == null)
            {
                GD.Print($"buffering coord2D {value}");
                _temp2D = value;
            }
            else
                _child?.Set("Coord2D", value);
        } 
    }
    Vector2 _temp2D;

    [Export]
    public Vector3 WrappedCoord3D 
    { 
        get => _child != null ? (Vector3)_child?.Get("Coord3D") : new Vector3()  ; 
        set
        {
            if(_child == null)
            {
                GD.Print($"buffering coord3D {value}");
                _temp3D = value;
            }
            else
                _child?.Set("Coord3D", value);
        } 
    }
    Vector3 _temp3D;
    Node3D _child = null;
	public override void _Ready()
    {
        _child = GetChild<Node3D>(0);
        GD.Print($"Instantiated child with name {_child?.Name}");
        WrappedCoord2D = _temp2D;
        WrappedCoord3D = _temp3D;
    }
}
```

* Instantiate in the Main scene
* Modify the values
* Hit the Remote Deploy button for the Meta Quest 3

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

The MRP requires installation of android templates + Godot XR Tools + Godot OpenXR Vendors plugin v5 + Godot Meta Toolkit (which are too big to upload with the minimal project)

[ScriptWrappingIssueCs.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27126204/ScriptWrappingIssueCs.zip)

**Edit** : Changed the getters. Also it seems the problem also applies to desktop export, see [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118996#issuecomment-4327991925)
